{
  "title": "SetSurrogateConfiguration",
  "messageId": "dc73",
  "isCommand": true,
  "description": "Sets the current surrogate configuration.  The expected\n\t\t\tresponse is a SetSurrogateConfigurationResponse message.  If the configuration is \n\t\t\tinvalid this should be indicated by the proper reason in the response message.  For \n\t\t\tlimit setting, the absence of a commanded change in limit along an axis (for example\n\t\t\tif you only set a Z maximum limit) does not cause a change in the uncommanded limit.  The \n\t\t\tMinimum and Maximum limits are defined using the relative pose, which is defined as a position \n\t\t\tand orientation relative to the Host Frame of reference, as defined in Section 3 Common \n\t\t\tConventions.",
  "type": "object",
